xnu 0229: the SP warm-up kernel every a730 command buffer has to start with

Turnip runs `cmdbuf_start_a725_quirk` at the start of every command buffer on
a725/a730 silicon: a compute kernel over the whole shader array (a multiply,
12 groups of 255 waves, 3072 invocations) plus the register writes that aim it
(HLSQ_INVALIDATE_CMD with all stages and both bindless sets,
HLSQ_CS_CNTL constlen 4 dword, SP_CS_CONFIG enabled, SP_CS_CTRL_REG0 MULTI +
THREAD128 + MERGEDREGS, shared size 2k, the NDRANGE 255x1x1, LAST_LOCAL_SIZE,
SP_CS_CNTL_0/_1 and SP_CS_OBJ first-exec pointing at the shader). Its
comment says "It is unknown what this workaround is for and what it fixes";
without it none of the renders reach memory -- every clear, state upload, draw
and shader output reads back zeros while the submissions complete and fence.

The port builds the stream once (a 1 KiB page in the CP's own address space at
0x303000, CP-visible with the same perms as the ring), and uc_submit emits a
CP_INDIRECT_BUFFER to it before the client indirect buffer, the way the
IFPC bracket was folded. cpuirk=0 leaves the streams alone.
